{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":317425,"ns":0,"title":"Circumstantial evidence","extract":"Circumstantial evidence is evidence that relies on an inference to connect it to a conclusion of fact, such as a fingerprint at the scene of a crime. By contrast, direct evidence supports the truth of an assertion directly, i.e.","description":"Evidence indirectly supporting conclusion","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}